### Structure breakdown per card:

```
<div class="card-grid">                <!-- Grid wrapper -->
  <div class="card-container">         <!-- Outer container (card) -->
    <div class="card-inner">           <!-- Inner wrapper -->
      <span class="card-label">Label</span>  <!-- Label span -->
      <p>Optional content</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  ...
</div>
```

### Key points:
- **Outer `div`** (`.card-container`) – handles the card's overall look (background, border, shadow, hover effects).
- **Inner `div`** (`.card-inner`) – separates content from the card's outer styling; can be used for padding or nested layout.
- **`span`** (`.card-label`) – the visible label; use `display: block` in CSS to make it behave like a block element inside the card.

The CSS grid handles responsive layouts automatically: cards reflow based on available width (thanks to `auto-fill` and `minmax`). You can add or remove cards without needing to change the grid config.

